@startuml backup-install
title ./backup.sh, at the root of the project : sets the backup configuration and its cron entry, nothing else

skinparam dpi 110
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ConditionStyle diamond
skinparam defaultFontName DejaVu Sans
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F7F7F7
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #555555
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF4D6
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #B8860B
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam SwimlaneBorderColor #999999
skinparam SwimlaneTitleFontStyle bold

|#FAFAFA|1. What is there|
start
if (Run as root?) then (no)
  #FFD9D9:Refuse: the cron entry
  cannot be written;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
if (Cron entry already\ninstalled?) then (no)
else (yes)
  :Show the current configuration
  time, backups kept, folders;
  if (Change it?) then (no, leave it)
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  if (Update or remove?) then (remove)
    #FFD9D9:Delete the cron entry
    and **backup.conf**
    Keep the archives
    The manager shows nothing anymore;
    stop
  else (update)
  endif
endif

|#FFF3E0|2. Ask, three questions|
#FFE2B8:**Time of the backup, every day**
on this server's clock
(Enter = 02:30);
#FFE2B8:**Backups kept at most**
one per day, so 5 days = 5 files
(Enter = 5);
#FFE2B8:**Folder where the archives go**
(Enter = ./backup);
note right
  Nothing else is asked
  Sending the archives to another
  server is set from the manager,
  never here
  On an update, Enter keeps
  the current value
  Each answer is asked again
  until it is valid
end note

|#F1F8F1|3. Write|
#D9F2D9:Write **backup.conf**
BACKUP_TIME, BACKUP_KEEP_DAYS, BACKUP_DIR
What the manager set for the off-site
copy is kept as it is;
#D9F2D9:Install or replace the cron entry
/etc/cron.d/simply-mailserver-backup
every day at HH:MM : scripts/backup.sh
every minute : scripts/backup.apply.sh;
#D9F2D9:Publish the configuration
for the manager to read;
:Show what was written;
stop
@enduml
